%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against adapters/core_data/caching.py
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> CLOSED

    CLOSED: <b>CLOSED</b> - normal
    CLOSED: every call goes through to the bank core
    CLOSED: results cached with a TTL

    OPEN: <b>OPEN</b> - upstream is down
    OPEN: fail INSTANTLY, do not even try
    OPEN: serve stale cache and SAY SO

    HALF: <b>cooldown elapsed</b>
    HALF: let one call through and see

    CLOSED --> OPEN : failures cross the threshold
    OPEN --> HALF : cooldown elapsed
    HALF --> CLOSED : it worked
    HALF --> OPEN : it failed again

    note right of OPEN
        WHY this matters more than it looks:
        without a breaker, a dead core costs
        a full timeout PER LOOKUP - six reads
        means six timeouts, and the brief is
        late for every single caller.
        With it, degradation costs microseconds.
    end note

    note right of CLOSED
        served_stale flag propagates all the way
        to the agent screen as CORE_DATA_STALE.
        An agent seeing old data deserves to
        know it is old. (D18)
    end note
